> Trying to deserialize { "number" : NaN } will be successful whereas { "number" : naN } will fail.

No, they need be inside quotes, otherwise the reader would throw invalid token:

```
var reader = new Utf8JsonReader(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("NaN"));
Console.WriteLine(reader.Read());
// throws: Unhandled exception. System.Text.Json.JsonReaderException: 'N' is an invalid start of a value. LineNumber: 0 | BytePositionInLine: 0.
```
